{"content": "That Day: The Fall of Shiganshina, Part 2 is the 2nd episode of the 1st season and the 2nd episode overall of the Attack on Titan anime, produced by Wit Studio and Production I.G.\n\nTitans continue to kill the citizens of Shiganshina as Eren, Mikasa, and Armin escape with their lives. After an Armored Titan breaks through the inner gate, Eren vows to kill all the Titans in the world. A year after Armin's grandfather perishes in an operation to retake Wall Maria, the three children join the military as part of the 104th Cadet Corps.\n\nAs crows begin to feed on the dead citizens of Shiganshina District, a religious man is frantically reciting words from his book. Townsfolk are screaming and running as the Titans roam the district, and the man is eventually confronted and eaten by a Titan, his book falling to the ground. A woman flees to a dark alley, covering her mouth, and is plucked from her spot, screaming.", "chunk_index": 0, "source_url": "https://attackontitan.fandom.com/wiki/That_Day:_The_Fall_of_Shiganshina,_Part_2", "source_title": "That Day: The Fall of Shiganshina, Part 2", "source_type": "episode", "episode_number": 2, "entity": null, "reveal_episode": 2, "embedding": [-0.0023486644495278597, 0.08188576996326447, 0.03321667015552521, 0.013322164304554462, 0.053216107189655304, 0.011335338465869427, 0.08200570940971375, 0.047276295721530914, 0.02607925795018673, 0.026022640988230705, 0.03754488006234169, 0.00303047732450068, 0.046299826353788376, -0.01779276132583618, -0.012603417038917542, -0.08537261188030243, -0.011528021655976772, 0.019387079402804375, 0.07023277878761292, 0.008976214565336704, -0.014951342716813087, -0.0016024868236854672, 0.004147584084421396, 0.04460357874631882, 0.04450410604476929, -0.027480602264404297, -0.009194303303956985, -0.03750060871243477, -0.053805749863386154, -0.03402296081185341, 0.07383108884096146, -0.0005776203470304608, -0.009753979742527008, 0.02706350013613701, -0.042721763253211975, 0.031543906778