{"content": "Recovering from his state of shock, Eren attacks Hannes for abandoning his mother. He insists that if given more time, his mother could have been saved. With Eren struggling to punch him again, Hannes explains that Eren did not have the strength to save his mother, further infuriating him. However, he then says that the reason he could not save Eren's mother was because he did not have the courage to face the Titan. As they are led toward Wall Maria, Mikasa's head begins to ache as she recalls a dead man and woman before remarking about the familiarity of this event.\n\nArmin is on a ship preparing to leave Shiganshina, scanning the crowds for Eren and Mikasa. He spots them in a large crowd of refugees, but refrains from calling them when he sees the look on their faces. His grandfather notes their faces as well, understanding that they must have felt some great amount of terror. A Garrison soldier shepherds a group of survivors through the gates, and takes charge in defending the ships used to escape the district. While he and his comrades fruitlessly defend the inner Wall, Hannes and another officer debate about whether they should close the gate and abandon their comrades, or leave them open for the comrades' retreat. This debate is short-lived as an Armored Titan appears, crashing through the inner Wall and killing its defenders. The gravity of the situation dawns on Eren when he realizes he can never go home again. Seeing the weakness of humanity, he vows to kill every last Titan in the world.", "chunk_index": 1, "source_url": "https://attackontitan.fandom.com/wiki/That_Day:_The_Fall_of_Shiganshina,_Part_2", "source_title": "That Day: The Fall of Shiganshina, Part 2", "source_type": "episode", "episode_number": 2, "entity": null, "reveal_episode": 2, "embedding": [0.01765170507133007, 0.11406075209379196, 0.08179746568202972, 0.03190065920352936, 0.10258115828037262, -0.0033436701633036137, 0.09443452954292297, 0.07393266260623932, 0.01117263920605